# AlphaBench — optional environment variables. Copy to .env and adjust as needed.
# NEVER commit the resulting .env file (it is already in .gitignore).
#
# No provider API key is required anywhere in this list: the yfinance and stooq
# providers this project actually uses (src/alphabench/data/providers/) need no
# credentials to pull free OHLCV history.

# --- Dashboard -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL the Streamlit dashboard calls for API requests. Read directly by
# src/alphabench/dashboard/app.py (os.getenv("API_URL", "http://localhost:8000")).
# Only needed to point a locally-running dashboard at a non-default API — the
# default already matches `make api` + `make dashboard` run together.
# API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- CI / keep-alive ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Not read from a local .env — set as GitHub Actions repository secrets instead
# (Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions). .github/workflows/keep-alive.yaml
# pings both services' health endpoints to blunt Render's free-tier cold start.
# DASHBOARD_URL falls back to the published dashboard URL if the secret is unset.
#   API_URL=https://alphabench.onrender.com
#   DASHBOARD_URL=https://alphabench-dashboard.onrender.com

# --- Experiment tracking -----------------------------------------------------------
# Standard MLflow variable, read by the mlflow library itself (not by this
# project's own code) inside training/train.py and training/train_xgboost.py.
# Unset, MLflow defaults to a local ./mlruns directory — gitignored, and not
# populated in this repo; see docs/TECH_STACK_AND_STRUCTURE.md section 2.2 for
# why no run history ships here and where the same evidence is instead
# committed. Point this at a remote tracking server to centralise runs across
# machines/sessions.
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=http://localhost:5000
